Figure 2 illustrates the *in vivo* biodistribution and clearance kinetics of Nano-11 nanoparticles after intramuscular injection in mice. Whole-mouse imaging (a) shows that fluorescently labeled Nano-11 remains primarily localized at the injection site over 21 days, with no evidence of systemic distribution. Dissected organs on day 21 (b) further confirm this local retention. Quantification of injection site fluorescence (c) reveals a rapid decrease initially, a slight increase on day 2, followed by a continuous decline, with approximately 20% of the original signal remaining after 21 days. This indicates Nano-11 is retained locally and cleared gradually.